\n1 |RWF0|NWF0|BWF0|QWF0|KWF0|BWF0|NWF0|RWF0| 1\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[P: a7-a5, P: a7-a6, P: b7-b5, P: b7-b6, N: b8-a6, N: b8-c6, P: c7-c5, P: c7-c6, P: d7-d5, P: d7-d6, P: e7-e5, P: e7-e6, P: f7-f5, P: f7-f6, P: g7-g5, P: g7-g6, N: g8-f6, N: g8-h6, P: h7-h5, P: h7-h6]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': 'Situation: White has advanced the g-pawn to g4 early, slightly weakening their king-side dark squares (f3/h3) and leaving the g-pawn potentially overextended. All other pieces are in the starting setup; it’s Black to play and we should claim central space and develop smoothly.\n\nEvaluation: Promising moves include **P: e7-e5** (best central claim and opens lines for bishop/queen), **N: g8-f6** (develops and hits g4/e4), and **P: g7-g6** (aiming for …Bg7 to pressure the long diagonal and target g4 indirectly). Among these, **…e5** is the most principled: it fights for the center immediately and prepares rapid development and potential kingside initiative versus White’s weakened g-file.\n\nReason: **P: e7-e5** maximizes winning chances by taking central space, enabling quick development (…Nf6, …Bc5/…Bb4+, …d5 ideas), and setting up pressure against White’s premature g-pawn push without committing to flank pawn moves.\n\nAnswer: P: e7-e5'}
